lling back to either one doesn't need change-manager approval.\n\nWhich should I do?\n1. Roll back `payments-api` to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back both\n\nOnce you choose, I'll do the rollback and open the SEV2 incident against that service, mentioning that the other one is also failing. If you'd like the on-call engineer paged now while you decide, I can open the SEV2 straight away, listing both services.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 282677, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 254847, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 282677, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 287285, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PUHuyfde9u2UL1wFfCArg6", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 291285, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PUHuyfde9u2UL1wFfCArg6", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 291285, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PUHuyfde9u2UL1wFfCArg6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 291285, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012stiWMLKQikDCEk9NWC46J", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 errors after deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (this morning's deploy) became unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18% errors, which looks like a down